3x = 23
[÷3] \frac{3x}{3} = \frac{23}{3}    (Divide both sides by 3.)
= 7\frac{2}{3}
Check: LHS = 3 × 7\frac{2}{3}
= 3 × \frac{23}{3}
= 23
= RHS

\frac{3x}{4} = 10
[×4] 3x = 40    (Multiply both sides by 4.)
[÷3] x = \frac{40}{3}    (Divide both sides by 3.)
= 13\frac{1}{3}
Check: LHS = \frac{3 × 13\frac{1}{3}}{4}
= \frac{40}{4}
= 10
= RHS
